<ontology/use_varnish_paint_lacquer/use_varnish_paint_lacquer__doc_prussian_blue__q1/#resource> dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (2nd ed., 1840; Project Gutenberg #44562), s.v. PRINTING INK" ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/44562> ;
    a <ontology/EvidenceQuote/#resource> ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Prussian Blue used in Varnish, Paint & Lacquer: Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (2nd ed., 1840; Project Gutenberg #44562), s.v. PRINTING INK"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "Put next of well ground indigo and prussian blue, each 2-1/2 ounces, into an earthen pan, sufficiently large to hold all the ink, along with 4 pounds of the best mineral lamp black, and 3-1/2 pounds of good vegetable lamp black; then add the warm varnish by slow degrees, carefully stirring, to produce a perfect incorporation of all the ingredients."@en ;
    <ontology/retrievalMode/#resource> "direct_sentence" .
